  "audit_groups": [
    {
      "topic": "Norm convention, empty divisor and sign",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The actual denominator convention gives log norm(1)=-delta for the degree-zero metric exp(delta). The source recursion subtracts that archimedean term and the divisor of 1 is empty. The single-slot change is therefore positive with coefficient one, including complex dimension zero."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Cone tensor cancellation",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The product of Euclidean block norms is smooth and positive on the nondegenerate cone, has multidegree all ones, obeys every required nonzero block scaling, and is zero off that cone. Thus tensoring converts cone equality into equality of the complete Hermitian data. Tensor additivity permits cancellation without an extra locality axiom."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Actual full locality",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The logarithmic ratio, extended by zero off the cone, is smooth where required and invariant under nonzero block scalings. At every source sheet point it vanishes if the metrics agree on the original variety. Single-slot variation and symmetry give exactly MetricLocalStatement; the empty tuple is tautological. No additive linearity of a possibly undefined ordinary integral is required: pointwise equality, zero and negation suffice."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Mixed energy factor and differential normalization",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "Telescoping has exactly n+1 mixed terms. The source complex Hessian is partial_z partial_bar_z, its normalized mixed discriminant gives n!(2/pi)^n times real volume, and dd^c=i/pi partial bar-partial has precisely this wedge density. Original sheet multiplicities and complex-place weights are retained. The half in the cusp comparison is exclusively psi-phi=U/2."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Smooth representatives and rational twists",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The source representatives preserve degree and restriction to the original variety. At smooth scales full locality identifies the rational twist with the tensor product. For p>=0 and q>=1, multilinearity gives the degree n+1 polynomial after division by q^(n+1); its constant term is exactly arLimFun, including p=0."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Vertical factors and remaining geometry",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The shared reference, finite vertical product and ample twist cancel in the normalized logarithmic ratio. Cancellation does not imply zero curvature for the common vertical metric. InterRes60-78 is an explicit separate compact-resolution integral bridge; its construction, component weights, vertical curvature and original geometric data remain open. No full Stokes estimate or whole proof node is claimed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Independent reproducible verification",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "Independently reran the supplied checker in offline mode: all 14 pinned blobs authenticated, 20 exterior-density cases, 56 independently differentiated Hessian entries, 340 cone cases, 153 telescope coefficients, 225 rational twists and sign/half/off-cone negative controls passed. These finite checks supplement the general mathematical proof and do not constitute a Lean build."
    }
